    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d868">

                <pb facs="0852" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg538"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.711/3</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-10-20">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">October 20, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 4:35 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>866. Sir Edward Grey has learned through commercial correspondence passing
                    through censor that arrangements appear to be in progress by which general
                    correspondence with Germany shall pass through American Consulate General at
                    Rotterdam. He asks me to bring this to your notice with a view to adequate steps
                    being taken to prevent the confidence of our consular officers being abused.
                    Despatch follows.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
